1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,010
Left: the booking page with Ada Alpha selected. Right: the booking page with Ben Bravo selected. Below: a terminal.

2
00:00:08,010 --> 00:00:19,997
Both users see 10 Available items (Ada) and 10 (Ben); price $100 on Ada's screen, $100 on Ben's.

3
00:00:19,997 --> 00:00:23,002
Ada and Ben pressed Hold on Item 1 at the same moment. Ada sees "Held" and "In your cart"; Ben sees "Someone else holds that item." and the item as "Restocking".

4
00:00:23,002 --> 00:00:24,507
Countdown running: Ada's cart reads "Item 1, 5s left".

5
00:00:24,507 --> 00:00:27,652
Countdown running: Ada's cart now reads "Item 1, 3s left"; Ben's item still shows Restocking.

6
00:00:27,652 --> 00:00:29,867
The hold ran out with no payment. Ada pressed Pay: "No active hold: your hold ended or you have none."

7
00:00:29,867 --> 00:00:38,077
Item 1 is "Available" again for Ada and "Available" for Ben; cart empty; price still $100.

8
00:00:38,077 --> 00:00:42,456
Ada holds Item 2: "Held", cart "Item 2, 8s left". Ben sees it as "Available".

9
00:00:42,456 --> 00:00:56,104
Ada paid: "Paid $100". Item 2 is "Available" again; price now $110. Ben's screen showed $110 0.9 s after Ada pressed Pay.

10
00:00:56,104 --> 00:01:00,421
Ben holds Item 3: "Held", cart "Item 3, 8s left". Price on his screen: $110.

11
00:01:00,421 --> 00:01:13,429
Ben paid: "Paid $110". Price is now $120 for Ben and $120 for Ada; Item 3 is "Available" again.

12
00:01:13,429 --> 00:01:18,441
Running the real test command in the terminal: node --test on tests/booking.test.mjs and tests/booking-hardening.test.mjs. Output streams live.

13
00:01:18,441 --> 00:01:32,446
Test run finished (exit 0): the terminal shows "tests 24", "pass 24", "fail 0" - 24 pass, 0 fail.

14
00:01:32,446 --> 00:01:39,447
Final state: Ada's and Ben's screens both show price $120; the terminal still shows "pass 24" and "fail 0".
